From ad7a135415cb476d12317ee384334cb0f176ac3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:44:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel material properties: tests written once,
 comparison with the generic interface

- the tests of the semantics of the generated functions are shared by the
  backends whose arrays are accessible by the host (tests.hxx, with
  batch.hxx building the data of a batch): statuses of the points, failures
  and unreliable results in the same batch, invalid results, errors of the
  batch, uniform and strided values, report function. The test of each
  backend gives its environment (memory, queue) and its specific tests;
- compare.cxx compares the evaluation on batches of points with the
  evaluation of the generic interface at each point, for the three out of
  bounds policies, contiguous, strided and uniform values, synchronous and
  asynchronous evaluations, in all the configurations (build-libraries.sh,
  compare-all.sh). The values are compared exactly with g++, clang++ and
  nvc++ on the host, up to 1e-13 with icpx and on devices;
- the refusal of a name containing `_generic_parallel` and the error
  reported for an invalid file of parameters are checked
  (check-refused-name.sh, test-invalid-parameters.cxx,
  stlpar-parunseq-gcc configuration);
- the selection of the memory and of the queue of the comparison of the
  behaviours is moved to runtime.hxx, shared by both comparisons;
- a material property with bounds and physical bounds on two arguments and
  on its output (BoundsOrderTest) checks the retained check (first failure,
  otherwise last warning, rank of the output), in tests.hxx and in the
  comparisons;
- the material property generated with the runtime checks disabled is run
  on stlpar, cuda, hip and sycl (test-no-runtime-checks.cxx, with the
  memory, the queue and the synchronization of runtime.hxx,
  build-no-runtime-checks.sh), as on openmp and openacc;
- the limit of the number of points is checked at 2^48 points, and the
  limit of the grid of the cuda and hip kernels without reading the arrays.
